// QA joint tmdb e2e (tmdb-enrichment 5.1, Tier 1 — the cross-module joint):
// REAL subprocess instances over the REAL api surface — the real server
// (cmd/mellifera with cmd's own closures: RequiredSecrets, the options write,
// IdentifyItem, the relay), the real tmdb plugin subprocess, real registry →
// queue → store chain — with exactly ONE stub: the upstream TMDB API, pinned
// through the plugin's sanctioned hermetic seam (MELLIFERA_TMDB_UPSTREAM —
// the MELLIFERA_SHIKIMORI_UPSTREAM precedent, plugins/tmdb/source.go). The
// stub's recorded requests double as the no-network proof AND as the
// substitution proof: the api_key literal can only arrive at the stub through
// the core-side resolveVariables seam (the plugin subprocess never sees the
// value). Five legs:
//
//	(a) TestQATmdbFilmEnrichmentJoint — a tv-library film; the api key
//	    configured through the REAL options write; the search passthrough; the
//	    item identify; the anchored /movie/{id} + /credits run; the served
//	    about + cast blocks.
//	(b) TestQATmdbEpisodeTitlesJoint — a serial-library series identified to
//	    a tmdb id; the anchored SERIES plan must carry the season extra (the
//	    document's own season fact) and its contributions must route onto the
//	    episode documents carrying title AND description.
//	(c) TestQATmdbUnconfiguredDormantJoint — the same binding with no secret:
//	    derivation derives nothing, the interactive surfaces answer the
//	    canonical 503, the aggregate carries the provided:false verdict.
//	(d) TestQATmdbItemIdentifyJoint — re-anchoring: identify to film A, then
//	    identify to film B; the re-derived run fetches BY the picked id and
//	    the namespace rebuilds fresh.
//	(e) TestQATmdbRelayDescriptorJoint — a network-class tmdb failure with
//	    the relay live hands out a job whose stored plan carries the RESOLVED
//	    api key, never the {server:api_key} placeholder.
//
// The expected values are re-derived independently of the plugin suites'
// fixtures (different ids, titles, dates — the no-coincidence discipline).
